@startuml
title Invoice Workflow — System Context and Use Cases (v3)
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false

actor Submitter
actor Approver
actor "Workflow operator" as Operator
actor "Academic evaluator" as Evaluator

rectangle "Invoice workflow application" {
  usecase "Submit invoice" as Submit
  usecase "View invoice status" as Status
  usecase "Review pending invoice" as Review
  usecase "Approve or reject" as Decide
  usecase "Configure workflow draft" as Configure
  usecase "Validate and activate revision" as Activate
  usecase "Inspect run trace" as Trace
  usecase "Compare execution modes" as Compare
}

Submitter --> Submit
Submitter --> Status
Approver --> Review
Approver --> Decide
Operator --> Configure
Operator --> Activate
Operator --> Trace
Evaluator --> Status
Evaluator --> Trace
Evaluator --> Compare

Decide ..> Review : <<include>>
Activate ..> Configure : <<include>>
Compare ..> Trace : <<include>>

note bottom of Submit
One bounded PDF and metadata payload.
No payment, OCR, or external email.
end note

note bottom of Compare
Same revision, input, decision,
and deterministic fault schedule.
end note

legend
Requirements v3 3.0 — architecture review view.
Logical roles only; authentication is outside scope.
No implementation or executable result is claimed.
endlegend
@enduml
